A.R.S runs third-party models and libraries that carry their own licences, which are NOT
covered by the terms above and which bind anyone who runs this software:

  Whisper large-v3-turbo (ASR)          MIT — OpenAI, via mlx-community
  Piper voices (TTS)                    per-voice; most CC BY 4.0 or MIT — see
                                        huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices
  Silero VAD                            MIT
  openWakeWord                          Apache-2.0
  Qwen3 (local reasoning, via Ollama)   Apache-2.0
  sentence-transformers / e5 models     MIT (multilingual-e5-small: MIT)
  FastAPI, pydantic, numpy, and the rest of the Python dependency tree: see each
  project's own licence.

Model weights are never committed to this repository (see .gitignore and CLAUDE.md
non-negotiable #8); they are fetched at setup time by scripts/fetch_voice_models.sh,
directly from their publishers and under their publishers' terms.
